[statement]
A dependency does not give way to the one candidate of a name packages
only provide, which neither the request nor the world names, as it gives
way to a provider among others
(`a-dependency-gives-way-to-one-of-two-providers-needing-it`): `a` needs
`w`, which only `c` 3 provides; `c` 3 needs `f`, and `f` 3, the best
candidate for `f`, forbids `w`. apk takes `f` 3 and refuses, though `f`
2 forbids nothing.

[repository]
P:f
V:3
D:!w

P:a
V:3
D:w

P:c
V:3
D:f
p:w=1

P:f
V:2

[request]
a

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   c-3:
|     breaks: f-3[!w]
|     satisfies: a-3[w]
refused
